msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:73
msgid "Show online availability on profile images"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:75
msgid ""
"You can show or hide :ref:`availability <end-user-guide/preferences/set-"
"your-status-availability:set your availability>` on profile pictures in "
"Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:79
msgid ""
"Select **Show online availability on profile images > Edit** to show or "
"hide availability in Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:86
msgid "Share last active time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:88
msgid ""
"By default, Mattermost shows when you were last online in your profile "
"and in direct message channel headers, unless your system admin has "
":ref:`disabled this option <administration-guide/configure/site-"
"configuration-settings:enable last active time>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:92
msgid ""
"Select **Share last active time > Edit** to show or hide when you were "
"last online in Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:99
msgid "Timezone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:101
msgid ""
"You can customize the timezone used for timestamps in Mattermost and in "
"email notifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:105
msgid "Select **Timezone > Edit** to select your timezone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:107
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.10, you can also select **Automatic** to set your "
"timezone automatically based on your computer's timezone settings. This "
"option is enabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:111
msgid ""
"Tap **Timezone** to set your timezone automatically based on your mobile "
"device preference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:114
msgid "Website link previews"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:116
msgid ""
"You can control whether website link previews in Mattermost show a "
"preview of the website content directly below the message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:120
msgid ""
"Your system admin must :ref:`enable this feature <administration-"
"guide/configure/site-configuration-settings:enable message link "
"previews>`. It's disabled by default. Once enabled, only the first web "
"link in a message creates a preview of the website."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:124
msgid ""
"Select **Website Link Previews > Edit** to show or hide website previews "
"in messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:131
msgid "Default appearance of image previews"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:133
msgid ""
"When messages in Mattermost include images, you can control whether an "
"image preview displays directly below the message for image attachments, "
"image link previews, and :ref:`in-line images <end-user-guide/collaborate"
"/format-messages:in-line images>` over 100px in height."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:137
msgid ""
"Select **Default Appearance of Image Previews > Edit** to expand or "
"collapse all image links and image attachments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:140
msgid ""
"This setting can also be controlled using the :doc:`slash commands "
"</integrations-guide/run-slash-commands>` ``/expand`` and ``/collapse``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:147
msgid "Message display"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:149
msgid "You can control how messages in a channel are displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:153
msgid "Select **Message Display > Edit** to display standard or compact messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:157
msgid ""
"**Compact** mode fits more messages on the screen by decreasing the "
"spacing around posts, collapsing link previews, and hiding thumbnails so "
"that only file names are shown. Some formatting types, such as block "
"quotes and headings, are also reduced in size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:159
msgid ""
"When you select **Compact**, usernames are colorized by default, and "
"username colors are consistent for all users. Disable the **Colorize "
"usernames** option to display all usernames in a single color instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:167
msgid "Click to open threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:169
msgid ""
"By default, Mattermost opens reply threads in the right pane when you "
"select any part of a message. You can change this default behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:173
msgid ""
"Select **Click to open threads > Edit** to disable the default behavior "
"of opening reply threads in the right pane automatically. You'll need to "
"select the replies count to open a reply thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:180
msgid "Channel display"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:182
msgid "You can control the width of the center channel area in Matermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:186
msgid ""
"Select **Channel Display  > Edit** to specify the center channel as fixed"
" width and centered, or full width."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:193
msgid "Quick reactions on messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:195
msgid ""
"By default, you can hover over messages to react using recently-used "
"emojis. You can hide your recently-used emojis instead if preferred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:199
msgid ""
"Select **Quick reactions on messages > Edit** to hide your recently-used "
"emojis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:206
msgid "Render emoticons as emojis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:208
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.10, you can choose whether to automatically convert "
"text emoticons to emoji characters in your messages. This feature is "
"enabled by default, so that text-based emoticons like ``:)`` or ``:D`` "
"are displayed as their corresponding emoji images. Disable this auto-"
"rendering if you prefer to keep emoticons as text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/preferences/manage-your-display-options.rst:212
msgid ""
"Select **Render emoticons as emojis > Edit** to disable automatic "
"conversion of emoticons to emojis in your messages."
msgstr ""

